lat":35.07979,"lng":-106.60629},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"albuquerque_wv_flying_star_cafe","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://flyingstarcafe.com/","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["flyingstarcafe","albuquerque"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"06:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"23:00"},null,null,{"open":"06:00","close":"23:00"}],"note":"Closed Fri, Sat"},"summary":"A local space age-themed chain with a wide variety of salads, sandwiches, entrees, New Mexican food, and superb desserts. Rated 'Best Bakery' in Albuquerque. Daily and weekly specials. Free wi-fi and comfy seating areas. Vast selection of magazines. Flying Star also operates the local Satellite Coffee chain, which has a great coffee selection and some of the same pastries you'll find at the Flying","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Albuquerque"},{"id":"albuquerque_wv_frontier_restaurant","areaId":"albuquerque","name":"Frontier Restaurant","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":35.08077,"lng":-106.61923},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"albuquerque_wv_frontier_restaurant","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.frontierrestaurant.com/","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["frontierrestaurant","albuquerque"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"05:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"05:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"05:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"05:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"05:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"05:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"05:00","close":"23:59"}]},"summary":"One of the most popular restaurants in Albuquerque; a big hangout for the college students at UNM. Good American and New Mexican food, the breakfast burrito here is one of the best in Albuquerque. The atmosphere is casual, and it's a great place to people-watch and witness a good cross-section of the city's population. If you can't make it to the Frontier, you can go to one of the several Golden P","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Albuquerque"},{"id":"albuquerque_wv_bob_s_burgers","areaId":"albuquerque","name":"Bob's Burgers","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":35.08448,"lng":-106.68836},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"albuquerque_wv_bob_s_burgers","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["bobsburgers","albuquerque"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"10:30","close":"21:00"},{"open":"10:30","close":"21:00"},{"open":"10:30","close":"21:00"},{"open":"10:30","close":"21:00"},{"open":"10:30","close":"21:00"},{"open":"10:30","close":"21:00"},{"open":"10:30","close":"21:00"}]},"summary":"A home-grown chain of burger stands with a New Mexican flair. The ones west of the river are owned by Bob, the ones east of the river by his son-in-law Clifford. Bob makes some of the hottest green chile sauce in the state; Clifford flat out tries to kill you. A \"chile-head\"'s paradise. Try a long chile-cheese dog with green sauce instead of traditional red.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Albuquerque"},{"id":"albuquerque_wv_banh_mi_coda","areaId":"albuquerque","name":"Banh Mi Coda","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":35.07454,"lng":-106.56822},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"albuquerque_wv_banh_mi_coda","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["banhmicoda","albuquerque"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Excellent Vietnamese sandwiches. Get the #6, grilled pork on a French style baguette with French-inspired style mayo (aioli), cucumber, cilantro, strips of pickled carrots, and slices of jalapeños. Bakery also carries various Vietnamese desserts, steamed sweet/glutinous rice with mung beans, and Vietnamese steamed pork sausages.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Albuquerque"},{"id":"albuquerque_wv_grandma_s_k_i_diner","areaId":"albuquerque","name":"Grandma's K&I Diner","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":35.05631,"lng":-106.6448},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"albuquerque_wv_grandma_s_k_i_diner","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["grandmaskidiner","albuquerque"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"06:00","close":"15:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"15:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"15:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"15:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"15:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"15:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"15:00"}]},"summary":"Enjoy some authentic Albuquerque cuisine, restaurant is best known for serving a fry covered, football sized burrito called the Travis. They can be ordered in eighths, quarters, halves or whole; consumption of an entire travis is sometimes used as a fraternity hazing. The breakfast skillet meals are wonderful.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Albuquerque"},{"id":"albuquerque_wv_saggio_s_pizza","areaId":"albuquerque","name":"Saggio's Pizza","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":35.08047,"lng":-106.61978},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"albuquerque_wv_saggio_s_pizza","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.saggios.com/","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["saggiospizza","albuquerque"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"08:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"},null,{"open":"08:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Closed Sat"},"summary":"Some of the best pizza in Albuquerque. The atmosphere is wonderful, with statues, murals, plants, and televisions everywhere. There is a sports bar in here, but the place is still very kid-friendly.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Albuquerque"},{"id":"albuquerque_wv_zinc_wine_bar_and_bistro",